-- title:
--   Base change isomorphism onto the K-span of an 𝔽ₚ-linear map
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $V$ a finite $\mathbb{Z}/p$-module (an additive commutative group with a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-module structure whose underlying type is finite), $K$ a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebra structure, and $W$ an additive commutative group carrying compatible $K$- and $\mathbb{Z}/p$-module structures (the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-action factoring through $K$ via the scalar-tower condition). Let $\Theta : V \to W$ be $\mathbb{Z}/p$-linear, and assume that the cardinality of $V$ equals $p^{\,d}$, where $d = \dim_K \operatorname{span}_K(\operatorname{range}\Theta)$ is the $K$-dimension of the $K$-submodule of $W$ generated by the image of $\Theta$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a $K$-linear isomorphism $$e : K \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p} V \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \operatorname{span}_K(\operatorname{range}\Theta)$$ such that for all $c \in K$ and $v \in V$ the element $e(c \otimes v)$, viewed in $W$, equals $c \cdot \Theta(v)$. Thus the canonical base-change extension of $\Theta$ is a $K$-linear isomorphism from $K \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p} V$ onto the $K$-span of the image of $\Theta$; in particular $\Theta$ is injective and sends any $\mathbb{Z}/p$-basis of $V$ to a $K$-linearly independent family.
--
--   A piece of linear algebra over $\mathbb{F}_p$: the numerical hypothesis $\#V = p^{\dim_K \operatorname{span}_K \Theta(V)}$ says exactly that $\Theta$ exhibits $V$ as an $\mathbb{F}_p$-structure on the $K$-span of its image. It is used in the comparison of a finite $\mathbb{F}_p$-space with the $K$-span of its image inside a space of differentials, in the argument supporting [`ModularCurve.exists_linearMap_injective_range_eq_dual_multiplicativeSubmodule_ssPolarDifferentials_of_jHNeronObjectAtP_of_twoCompRegularDifferentials_of_ordinary_torusCoords_of_mem_infSubgroup`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_linearMap_injective_range_eq_dual_multiplicativeSubmodule_ssPolarDifferentials_of_jHNeronObjectAtP_of_twoCompRegularDifferentials_of_ordinary_torusCoords_of_mem_infSubgroup).
